In 1959 a lot of people were killing time. Kit and Holly were killing people.

2
00:09:53,684 --> 00:09:59,684
Badlands is a crime, drama, romance film directed by Terrence Malick.

3
00:14:50,526 --> 00:14:56,526
An impressionable teenage girl from a dead-end town and her older greaser
boyfriend embark on a killing spree in the South Dakota badlands.

4
00:19:47,368 --> 00:19:53,368
Kit Carruthers, played by Martin Sheen.

5
00:24:44,210 --> 00:24:50,210
Holly Sargis, played by Sissy Spacek.

6
00:29:41,052 --> 00:29:47,052
Holly's Father, played by Warren Oates.

7
00:34:37,894 --> 00:34:43,894
Cato, played by Ramon Bieri.

8
00:39:34,736 --> 00:39:40,736
Deputy, played by Alan Vint.

9
00:44:31,578 --> 00:44:37,578
Sheriff, played by Gary Littlejohn.

10
00:49:28,421 --> 00:49:34,421
Badlands is a 1973 American neo-noir period crime drama film written,
produced and directed by Terrence Malick, in his directorial debut.

11
00:54:25,263 --> 00:54:31,263
The film stars Martin Sheen and Sissy Spacek, and follows Holly Sargis (Spacek), a 15-year
old who goes on a killing spree with her partner, Kit Carruthers (Sheen).

12
00:59:22,105 --> 00:59:28,105
The film also stars Warren Oates and Ramon Bieri.

13
01:04:18,947 --> 01:04:24,947
While the story is fictional, it is loosely based on the real-life murder spree of
Charles Starkweather and his girlfriend, Caril Ann Fugate, in 1958.

14
01:09:15,789 --> 01:09:21,789
Badlands was released in 1973 to positive reviews from critics, who particularly praised its
cinematography, soundtrack—which includes pieces by Carl Orff—and the lead performances.

15
01:14:12,631 --> 01:14:18,631
At the 28th British Academy Film Awards, Spacek was nominated for the Most Promising Newcomer to Leading Film
Roles award, and Sheen won the Best Actor award at the San Sebastián International Film Festival.

16
01:19:09,473 --> 01:19:15,473
In 1993, the film was selected for preservation in the United States National Film Registry by the
Library of Congress as being "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant".

17
01:24:06,315 --> 01:24:12,315
The film explores themes of mass murder, based on true
story, fugitive, on the run, on the road.

18
01:29:03,157 --> 01:29:09,157
The tone is emotional.
